cards.questionText:
Discuss the importance of ethnic identity in the context of recent global developments.
Your answer might include the following:
• Rise of nationalism;
• Terrorist attacks;
• Imagined community;
• Migration;
• Us and them;
• Brexit / recent United States policies.

Article 12 of the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child (UNCRC) states that children
have the right to say what they think about matters that affect them and that their opinions
should be taken into consideration, depending on their age and level of maturity.
Drawing on your own experiences and on relevant research findings, discuss whether this right
is enjoyed by the young people of Ireland at school and/or local and/or national level.
Your answer might include the following:
• Decision‐making processes;
• Representative bodies of young people;
• Do all young people enjoy this right equally?
• Right holder / right bearer;
• Role of the Irish state;
• Challenges to the implementation of this right;
• Recommendations for further improvements in supporting / implementing this right.

Henderson Island
– an uninhabited, remote island littered with almost 38 million pieces of plastic
The amount of plastic dumped in the world’s oceans is now a serious threat to the environment.
Discuss how local initiatives and your own purchases can contribute to or challenge the growing
issue of global waste.
Your answer might include the following:
• Throw‐away society;
• Ethical consumerism;
• Local community action;
• Political initiatives, e.g. levy on disposable coffee cups (tax);
• European Union, e.g. Plastics Strategy;
• United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (Goal 13).

Discuss the power/responsibility of those who work in the media.
You may use the following phrases in your essay:
• Making or reporting the news;
• Different platforms (traditional, new and
social media);
• Getting people to act in ways they would not
otherwise act; being able to shape ideas;
• Fake news/bias/opinion;
• Disinformation/misinformation;
• News corporations; control; ownership;
• Key thinker e.g. Noam Chomsky.
